@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1414 = private unnamed_addr constant [402 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `trio.sleep(0)` or `anyio.sleep(0)`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`trio.sleep(0)` is equivalent to calling `trio.lowlevel.checkpoint()`.\0AHowever, the latter better conveys the intent of the code.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport trio\0A\0A\0Aasync def func():\0A    await trio.sleep(0)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport trio\0A\0A\0Aasync def func():\0A    await trio.lowlevel.checkpoint()\0A```\0A", align 1
