@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1421 = private unnamed_addr constant [669 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks that async functions do not open files with blocking methods like `open`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ABlocking an async function via a blocking call will block the entire\0Aevent loop, preventing it from executing other tasks while waiting for the\0Acall to complete, negating the benefits of asynchronous programming.\0A\0AInstead of making a blocking call, use an equivalent asynchronous library\0Aor function.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aasync def foo():\0A    with open(\22bar.txt\22) as f:\0A        contents = f.read()\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport anyio\0A\0A\0Aasync def foo():\0A    async with await anyio.open_file(\22bar.txt\22) as f:\0A        contents = await f.read()\0A```\0A", align 1
