@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1432 = private unnamed_addr constant [2006 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of weak or broken cryptographic hash functions in\0A`hashlib` and `crypt` libraries.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWeak or broken cryptographic hash functions may be susceptible to\0Acollision attacks (where two different inputs produce the same hash) or\0Apre-image attacks (where an attacker can find an input that produces a\0Agiven hash). This can lead to security vulnerabilities in applications\0Athat rely on these hash functions.\0A\0AAvoid using weak or broken cryptographic hash functions in security\0Acontexts. Instead, use a known secure hash function such as SHA256.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport hashlib\0A\0A\0Adef certificate_is_valid(certificate: bytes, known_hash: str) -> bool:\0A    hash = hashlib.md5(certificate).hexdigest()\0A    return hash == known_hash\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport hashlib\0A\0A\0Adef certificate_is_valid(certificate: bytes, known_hash: str) -> bool:\0A    hash = hashlib.sha256(certificate).hexdigest()\0A    return hash == known_hash\0A```\0A\0Aor add `usedforsecurity=False` if the hashing algorithm is not used in a security context, e.g.\0Aas a non-cryptographic one-way compression function:\0A```python\0Aimport hashlib\0A\0A\0Adef certificate_is_valid(certificate: bytes, known_hash: str) -> bool:\0A    hash = hashlib.md5(certificate, usedforsecurity=False).hexdigest()\0A    return hash == known_hash\0A```\0A\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `hashlib` \E2\80\94 Secure hashes and message digests](https://docs.python.org/3/library/hashlib.html)\0A- [Python documentation: `crypt` \E2\80\94 Function to check Unix passwords](https://docs.python.org/3/library/crypt.html)\0A- [Python documentation: `FIPS` - FIPS compliant hashlib implementation](https://docs.python.org/3/library/hashlib.html#hashlib.algorithms_guaranteed)\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-327](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/327.html)\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-328](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/328.html)\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-916](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/916.html)\0A", align 1
