@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1439 = private unnamed_addr constant [579 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for HTTPS requests that disable SSL certificate checks.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf SSL certificates are not verified, an attacker could perform a \22man in\0Athe middle\22 attack by intercepting and modifying traffic between the client\0Aand server.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport requests\0A\0Arequests.get(\22https://www.example.com\22, verify=False)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport requests\0A\0Arequests.get(\22https://www.example.com\22)  # By default, `verify=True`.\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-295](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/295.html)\0A", align 1
