@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1452 = private unnamed_addr constant [36 x i8] c"subprocess-without-shell-equals-true", align 1
@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1453 = private unnamed_addr constant [699 x i8] c"## What it does\0ACheck for method calls that initiate a subprocess without a shell.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AStarting a subprocess without a shell can prevent attackers from executing\0Aarbitrary shell commands; however, it is still error-prone. Consider\0Avalidating the input.\0A\0A## Known problems\0AProne to false positives as it is difficult to determine whether the\0Apassed arguments have been validated ([#4045]).\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport subprocess\0A\0Acmd = input(\22Enter a command: \22).split()\0Asubprocess.run(cmd)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `subprocess` \E2\80\94 Subprocess management](https://docs.python.org/3/library/subprocess.html)\0A\0A[#4045]: https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/4045\0A", align 1
