@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1470 = private unnamed_addr constant [31 x i8] c"start-process-with-partial-path", align 1
@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1471 = private unnamed_addr constant [726 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the starting of a process with a partial executable path.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AStarting a process with a partial executable path can allow attackers to\0Aexecute an arbitrary executable by adjusting the `PATH` environment variable.\0AConsider using a full path to the executable instead.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport subprocess\0A\0Asubprocess.Popen([\22ruff\22, \22check\22, \22file.py\22])\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport subprocess\0A\0Asubprocess.Popen([\22/usr/bin/ruff\22, \22check\22, \22file.py\22])\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `subprocess.Popen()`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/subprocess.html#subprocess.Popen)\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-426](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/426.html)\0A", align 1
