@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1475 = private unnamed_addr constant [541 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for possible wildcard injections in calls to `subprocess.Popen()`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWildcard injections can lead to unexpected behavior if unintended files are\0Amatched by the wildcard. Consider using a more specific path instead.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport subprocess\0A\0Asubprocess.Popen([\22chmod\22, \22777\22, \22*.py\22])\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport subprocess\0A\0Asubprocess.Popen([\22chmod\22, \22777\22, \22main.py\22])\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-78](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)\0A", align 1
