@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1502 = private unnamed_addr constant [790 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the presence of debugger calls and imports.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ADebugger calls and imports should be used for debugging purposes only. The\0Apresence of a debugger call or import in production code is likely a\0Amistake and may cause unintended behavior, such as exposing sensitive\0Ainformation or causing the program to hang.\0A\0AInstead, consider using a logging library to log information about the\0Aprogram's state, and writing tests to verify that the program behaves\0Aas expected.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef foo():\0A    breakpoint()\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `pdb` \E2\80\94 The Python Debugger](https://docs.python.org/3/library/pdb.html)\0A- [Python documentation: `logging` \E2\80\94 Logging facility for Python](https://docs.python.org/3/library/logging.html)\0A", align 1
