@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1513 = private unnamed_addr constant [583 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the use of `fields = \22__all__\22` in Django `ModelForm`\0Aclasses.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf a `ModelForm` includes the `fields = \22__all__\22` attribute, any new\0Afield that is added to the model will automatically be exposed for\0Amodification.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom django.forms import ModelForm\0A\0A\0Aclass PostForm(ModelForm):\0A    class Meta:\0A        model = Post\0A        fields = \22__all__\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom django.forms import ModelForm\0A\0A\0Aclass PostForm(ModelForm):\0A    class Meta:\0A        model = Post\0A        fields = [\22title\22, \22content\22]\0A```\0A", align 1
