@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1517 = private unnamed_addr constant [720 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks that a `__str__` method is defined in Django models.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ADjango models should define a `__str__` method to return a string representation\0Aof the model instance, as Django calls this method to display the object in\0Athe Django Admin and elsewhere.\0A\0AModels without a `__str__` method will display a non-meaningful representation\0Aof the object in the Django Admin.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom django.db import models\0A\0A\0Aclass MyModel(models.Model):\0A    field = models.CharField(max_length=255)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom django.db import models\0A\0A\0Aclass MyModel(models.Model):\0A    field = models.CharField(max_length=255)\0A\0A    def __str__(self):\0A        return f\22{self.field}\22\0A```\0A", align 1
