@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1536 = private unnamed_addr constant [29 x i8] c"explicit-string-concatenation", align 1
@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1537 = private unnamed_addr constant [508 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for string literals that are explicitly concatenated (using the\0A`+` operator).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AFor string literals that wrap across multiple lines, implicit string\0Aconcatenation within parentheses is preferred over explicit\0Aconcatenation using the `+` operator, as the former is more readable.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Az = (\0A    \22The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy \22\0A    + \22dog\22\0A)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Az = (\0A    \22The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy \22\0A    \22dog\22\0A)\0A```\0A", align 1
