@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1558 = private unnamed_addr constant [355 x i8] c"## What it does\0ARemoves ellipses (`...`) in otherwise non-empty class bodies.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAn ellipsis in a class body is only necessary if the class body is\0Aotherwise empty. If the class body is non-empty, then the ellipsis\0Ais redundant.\0A\0A## Example\0A```pyi\0Aclass Foo:\0A    ...\0A    value: int\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```pyi\0Aclass Foo:\0A    value: int\0A```\0A", align 1
