@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1669 = private unnamed_addr constant [16 x i8] c"os-path-splitext", align 1
@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1670 = private unnamed_addr constant [1906 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `os.path.splitext`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`pathlib` offers a high-level API for path manipulation, as compared to\0Athe lower-level API offered by `os.path`. When possible, using `Path` object\0Amethods such as `Path.suffix` and `Path.stem` can improve readability over\0Athe `os.path` module's counterparts (e.g., `os.path.splitext()`).\0A\0A`os.path.splitext()` specifically returns a tuple of the file root and\0Aextension (e.g., given `splitext('/foo/bar.py')`, `os.path.splitext()`\0Areturns `(\22foo/bar\22, \22.py\22)`. These outputs can be reconstructed through a\0Acombination of `Path.suffix` (`\22.py\22`), `Path.stem` (`\22bar\22`), and\0A`Path.parent` (`\22foo\22`).\0A\0A## Examples\0A```python\0Aimport os\0A\0A(root, ext) = os.path.splitext(\22foo/bar.py\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom pathlib import Path\0A\0Apath = Path(\22foo/bar.py\22)\0Aroot = path.parent / path.stem\0Aext = path.suffix\0A```\0A\0A## Known issues\0AWhile using `pathlib` can improve the readability and type safety of your code,\0Ait can be less performant than the lower-level alternatives that work directly with strings,\0Aespecially on older versions of Python.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `Path.suffix`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/pathlib.html#pathlib.PurePath.suffix)\0A- [Python documentation: `Path.suffixes`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/pathlib.html#pathlib.PurePath.suffixes)\0A- [Python documentation: `os.path.splitext`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.path.html#os.path.splitext)\0A- [PEP 428 \E2\80\93 The pathlib module \E2\80\93 object-oriented filesystem paths](https://peps.python.org/pep-0428/)\0A- [Correspondence between `os` and `pathlib`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/pathlib.html#correspondence-to-tools-in-the-os-module)\0A- [Why you should be using pathlib](https://treyhunner.com/2018/12/why-you-should-be-using-pathlib/)\0A- [No really, pathlib is great](https://treyhunner.com/2019/01/no-really-pathlib-is-great/)\0A", align 1
