@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1678 = private unnamed_addr constant [570 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of the `py.path` library.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `py.path` library is in maintenance mode. Instead, prefer the standard\0Alibrary's `pathlib` module, or third-party modules like `path` (formerly\0A`py.path`).\0A\0A## Examples\0A```python\0Aimport py.path\0A\0Ap = py.path.local(\22/foo/bar\22).join(\22baz/qux\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom pathlib import Path\0A\0Ap = Path(\22/foo/bar\22) / \22bar\22 / \22qux\22\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `Pathlib`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/pathlib.html)\0A- [Path repository](https://github.com/jaraco/path)\0A", align 1
@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1679 = private unnamed_addr constant [55 x i8] c"`py.path` is in maintenance mode, use `pathlib` instead", align 1
