@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1685 = private unnamed_addr constant [16 x i8] c"unsorted-imports", align 1
@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1686 = private unnamed_addr constant [804 x i8] c"## What it does\0ADe-duplicates, groups, and sorts imports based on the provided `isort` settings.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AConsistency is good. Use a common convention for imports to make your code\0Amore readable and idiomatic.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport pandas\0Aimport numpy as np\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport numpy as np\0Aimport pandas\0A```\0A\0A## Preview\0AWhen [`preview`](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/preview/) mode is enabled, Ruff applies a stricter criterion\0Afor determining whether an import should be classified as first-party.\0ASpecifically, for an import of the form `import foo.bar.baz`, Ruff will\0Acheck that `foo/bar`, relative to a [user-specified `src`](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/settings/#src) directory, contains either\0Athe directory `baz` or else a file with the name `baz.py` or `baz.pyi`.\0A", align 1
