@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1721 = private unnamed_addr constant [717 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for lowercase imports that are aliased to non-lowercase names.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 8] recommends naming conventions for classes, functions,\0Aconstants, and more. The use of inconsistent naming styles between\0Aimport and alias names may lead readers to expect an import to be of\0Aanother type (e.g., confuse a Python class with a constant).\0A\0AImport aliases should thus follow the same naming style as the member\0Abeing imported.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom example import myclassname as MyClassName\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom example import myclassname\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.ignore-names`\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.extend-ignore-names`\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/\0A", align 1
