@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1727 = private unnamed_addr constant [34 x i8] c"non-lowercase-variable-in-function", align 1
@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1728 = private unnamed_addr constant [792 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the use of non-lowercase variable names in functions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 8] recommends that all function variables use lowercase names:\0A\0A> Function names should be lowercase, with words separated by underscores as necessary to\0A> improve readability. Variable names follow the same convention as function names. mixedCase\0A> is allowed only in contexts where that's already the prevailing style (e.g. threading.py),\0A> to retain backwards compatibility.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef my_function(a):\0A    B = a + 3\0A    return B\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef my_function(a):\0A    b = a + 3\0A    return b\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.ignore-names`\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.extend-ignore-names`\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#function-and-variable-names\0A", align 1
