@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1750 = private unnamed_addr constant [29 x i8] c"no-space-after-inline-comment", align 1
@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1751 = private unnamed_addr constant [462 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks if one space is used after inline comments.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAn inline comment is a comment on the same line as a statement.\0A\0APer [PEP 8], inline comments should start with a # and a single space.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Ax = x + 1  #Increment x\0Ax = x + 1  #  Increment x\0Ax = x + 1  # \\xa0Increment x\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Ax = x + 1  # Increment x\0Ax = x + 1    # Increment x\0A```\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#comments\0A", align 1
