@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1754 = private unnamed_addr constant [28 x i8] c"no-space-after-block-comment", align 1
@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1755 = private unnamed_addr constant [559 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for block comments that lack a single space after the leading `#` character.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APer [PEP 8], \22Block comments generally consist of one or more paragraphs built\0Aout of complete sentences, with each sentence ending in a period.\22\0A\0ABlock comments should start with a `#` followed by a single space.\0A\0AShebangs (lines starting with `#!`, at the top of a file) are exempt from this\0Arule.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0A#Block comment\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A# Block comment\0A```\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#comments\0A", align 1
@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1756 = private unnamed_addr constant [36 x i8] c"Block comment should start with `# `", align 1
