@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1788 = private unnamed_addr constant [20 x i8] c"triple-single-quotes", align 1
@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1789 = private unnamed_addr constant [992 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for docstrings that use `'''triple single quotes'''` instead of\0A`\22\22\22triple double quotes\22\22\22`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 257](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/#what-is-a-docstring) recommends\0Athe use of `\22\22\22triple double quotes\22\22\22` for docstrings, to ensure\0Aconsistency.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef kos_root():\0A    '''Return the pathname of the KOS root directory.'''\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef kos_root():\0A    \22\22\22Return the pathname of the KOS root directory.\22\22\22\0A```\0A\0A## Formatter compatibility\0AWe recommend against using this rule alongside the [formatter]. The\0Aformatter enforces consistent quotes, making the rule redundant.\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [NumPy Style Guide](https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html)\0A- [Google Python Style Guide - Docstrings](https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#38-comments-and-docstrings)\0A\0A[formatter]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter/\0A", align 1
