@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1813 = private unnamed_addr constant [527 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for invalid assignments to `__all__`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIn Python, `__all__` should contain a sequence of strings that represent\0Athe names of all \22public\22 symbols exported by a module.\0A\0AAssigning anything other than a `tuple` or `list` of strings to `__all__`\0Ais invalid.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0A__all__ = \22Foo\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A__all__ = (\22Foo\22,)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: The `import` statement](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#the-import-statement)\0A", align 1
