@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1821 = private unnamed_addr constant [825 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for variables defined in `for`, `try`, `with` statements\0Athat redefine function parameters.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ARedefined variables can cause unexpected behavior because of overridden function parameters.\0AIf nested functions are declared, an inner function's body can override an outer function's parameters.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef show(host_id=10.11):\0A    for host_id, host in [[12.13, \22Venus\22], [14.15, \22Mars\22]]:\0A        print(host_id, host)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef show(host_id=10.11):\0A    for inner_host_id, host in [[12.13, \22Venus\22], [14.15, \22Mars\22]]:\0A        print(host_id, inner_host_id, host)\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.dummy-variable-rgx`\0A\0A## References\0A- [Pylint documentation](https://pylint.readthedocs.io/en/latest/user_guide/messages/refactor/redefined-argument-from-local.html)\0A", align 1
