@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1826 = private unnamed_addr constant [17 x i8] c"useless-with-lock", align 1
@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1827 = private unnamed_addr constant [799 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for lock objects that are created and immediately discarded in\0A`with` statements.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ACreating a lock (via `threading.Lock` or similar) in a `with` statement\0Ahas no effect, as locks are only relevant when shared between threads.\0A\0AInstead, assign the lock to a variable outside the `with` statement,\0Aand share that variable between threads.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport threading\0A\0Acounter = 0\0A\0A\0Adef increment():\0A    global counter\0A\0A    with threading.Lock():\0A        counter += 1\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport threading\0A\0Acounter = 0\0Alock = threading.Lock()\0A\0A\0Adef increment():\0A    global counter\0A\0A    with lock:\0A        counter += 1\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `Lock Objects`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/threading.html#lock-objects)\0A", align 1
