@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1835 = private unnamed_addr constant [411 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `io.open`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIn Python 3, `io.open` is an alias for `open`. Prefer using `open` directly,\0Aas it is more idiomatic.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport io\0A\0Awith io.open(\22file.txt\22) as f:\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Awith open(\22file.txt\22) as f:\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `io.open`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/io.html#io.open)\0A", align 1
