@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1847 = private unnamed_addr constant [440 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for literals that are similar to constants in `math` module.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AHard-coding mathematical constants like \CF\80 increases code duplication,\0Areduces readability, and may lead to a lack of precision.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0AA = 3.141592 * r**2\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0AA = math.pi * r**2\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `math` constants](https://docs.python.org/3/library/math.html#constants)\0A", align 1
