@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1854 = private unnamed_addr constant [753 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for consecutive `global` (or `nonlocal`) statements.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `global` and `nonlocal` keywords accepts multiple comma-separated names.\0AInstead of using multiple `global` (or `nonlocal`) statements for separate\0Avariables, you can use a single statement to declare multiple variables at\0Aonce.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef func():\0A    global x\0A    global y\0A\0A    print(x, y)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef func():\0A    global x, y\0A\0A    print(x, y)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: the `global` statement](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#the-global-statement)\0A- [Python documentation: the `nonlocal` statement](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#the-nonlocal-statement)\0A", align 1
