@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1860 = private unnamed_addr constant [628 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for enum classes which are also decorated with `@dataclass`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ADecorating an enum with `@dataclass()` does not cause any errors at runtime,\0Abut may cause erroneous results:\0A\0A```python\0A@dataclass\0Aclass E(Enum):\0A    A = 1\0A    B = 2\0A\0Aprint(E.A == E.B)  # True\0A```\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Afrom dataclasses import dataclass\0Afrom enum import Enum\0A\0A\0A@dataclass\0Aclass E(Enum): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Afrom enum import Enum\0A\0A\0Aclass E(Enum): ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Enum HOWTO &sect; Dataclass support](https://docs.python.org/3/howto/enum.html#dataclass-support)\0A", align 1
