@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1863 = private unnamed_addr constant [33 x i8] c"explicit-f-string-type-conversion", align 1
@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1864 = private unnamed_addr constant [598 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `str()`, `repr()`, and `ascii()` as explicit type\0Aconversions within f-strings.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0Af-strings support dedicated conversion flags for these types, which are\0Amore succinct and idiomatic.\0A\0ANote that, in many cases, calling `str()` within an f-string is\0Aunnecessary and can be removed entirely, as the value will be converted\0Ato a string automatically, the notable exception being for classes that\0Aimplement a custom `__format__` method.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aa = \22some string\22\0Af\22{repr(a)}\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aa = \22some string\22\0Af\22{a!r}\22\0A```\0A", align 1
