@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1871 = private unnamed_addr constant [37 x i8] c"invalid-formatter-suppression-comment", align 1
@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1872 = private unnamed_addr constant [800 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for formatter suppression comments that are ineffective or incompatible\0Awith Ruff's formatter.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ASuppression comments that do not actually prevent formatting could cause unintended changes\0Awhen the formatter is run.\0A\0A## Example\0AIn the following example, all suppression comments would cause\0Aa rule violation.\0A\0A```python\0Adef decorator():\0A    pass\0A\0A\0A@decorator\0A# fmt: off\0Adef example():\0A    if True:\0A        # fmt: skip\0A        expression = [\0A            # fmt: off\0A            1,\0A            2,\0A        ]\0A        # yapf: disable\0A    # fmt: on\0A    # yapf: enable\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0A\0AThis fix is always marked as unsafe because it deletes the invalid suppression comment,\0Arather than trying to move it to a valid position, which the user more likely intended.\0A\0A", align 1
